    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "narration": {
    "en": "One way to solve it is by factorising. For x squared minus 5 x plus 6, the factors are x minus 2 and x minus 3. The product is zero when one factor is zero, so x is 2 or x is 3."
   },
   "actions": [
    {
     "do": "write",
