     "at": 0.5
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "narration": {
    "en": "The part under the square root, b squared minus 4 a c, is the discriminant. It tells us the kind of roots. If it is more than zero there are two different real roots, if it is zero the roots are equal, and if it is less than zero there are no real roots."
   },
